# Backend Unit vs Integration Tests

**Directories are the source of truth** — not pytest markers. Place tests under `backend/src/tests/unit/**` or `backend/src/tests/integration/**` and mirror domain folders (`api/`, `services/`, `providers/`, …). Shared helpers live in `backend/src/tests/support/` (sibling to both trees, never under `unit/` or `integration/`).

## Unit (`tests/unit/**`)

- No Postgres, no `prepare_db`, no `async_client`, no ASGI/httpx against the app
- Pure logic (parsers, slug helpers, scoring) or services with mocked/fake DAOs only
- May import shared fakes from `tests/support/`

## Integration (`tests/integration/**`)

- Uses **any** of: `prepare_db`, `async_client`, real DB/DAO/session, HTTP route tests
- **Ambiguous → integration** (safe default)
- All former `api/` tests; `migrations/`, DB-heavy `scripts/`, `tasks/`, `models/`

## Forbidden

- `prepare_db` or `async_client` under `unit/` — collection guard fails fast
- `@pytest.mark.integration` as primary classifier — directories decide type

## Run (Docker-first — see `.cursor/tech.md`)

| Target | Scope |
|--------|--------|
| `make backend-test-unit` | `src/tests/unit` — Postgres **not** required |
| `make backend-test-integration` | `src/tests/integration` — Postgres required |
| `make backend-test` | Both sequentially (full suite) |
| `make backend-test-one target=…` | Path must include `unit/` or `integration/` prefix |

Until split targets land in the Makefile, use `make backend-test`; table above is the approved contract.

## Path examples

❌ **BAD:** `backend/src/tests/services/test_scoring.py` (legacy flat layout)  
✅ **GOOD:** `backend/src/tests/unit/services/taste_quiz/test_scoring.py`

❌ **BAD:** `backend/src/tests/unit/api/test_public_routes.py` (API = integration)  
✅ **GOOD:** `backend/src/tests/integration/api/test_public_routes.py`

❌ **BAD:** unit test requesting `prepare_db`  
✅ **GOOD:** mock DAO in unit; move to `integration/services/` if real DB needed

